From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mm: lower unreclaimable floor for microVM overcommit

Even with reclaim-allowed balloon allocation and drop-caches-on-stall,
three stock defaults keep MiBs stranded on the host behind the balloon:

- min_free_kbytes watermarks are unballoonable reserves. Quarter the
  stock sqrt(lowmem*16) curve (128-1024MB guests: ~2-3 MiB freed).
  Fresh microVMs boot with empty caches so the smaller reserve is safe.
  Tunable at runtime via /proc/sys/vm/min_free_kbytes.
- vfs_cache_pressure 100 -> 1000. Dentry/inode slab is otherwise
  unballoonable and strands MiBs on file-heavy guests; 10x pressure
  converts it into balloonable memory faster.
  Tunable at runtime via /proc/sys/vm/vfs_cache_pressure.
- dirty ratios floored (background 10 -> 1, ratio 20 -> 2) so dirty
  pages start writeback sooner and become clean (hence droppable and
  balloonable) sooner instead of pinning host memory.
  Tunable at runtime via /proc/sys/vm/dirty_{background_,}ratio.

Signed-off-by: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
---
fs/dcache.c          | 8 +++++++-
mm/page-writeback.c  | 9 +++++++--
mm/page_alloc.c      | 12 +++++++++---
 3 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/dcache.c b/fs/dcache.c
index 123456789030..123456789031 100644
--- a/fs/dcache.c
+++ b/fs/dcache.c
@@ -73,7 +73,13 @@
  * If no ancestor relationship:
  * arbitrary, since it's serialized on rename_lock
  */
-static int sysctl_vfs_cache_pressure __read_mostly = 100;
+/*
+ * MicroVM: reclaim dentries/inodes 10x more aggressively. Dentry/inode
+ * slab is otherwise unballoonable and strands MiBs on the host; higher
+ * pressure converts it into balloonable memory faster.
+ * (Tunable at runtime via /proc/sys/vm/vfs_cache_pressure.)
+ */
+static int sysctl_vfs_cache_pressure __read_mostly = 1000;
 static int sysctl_vfs_cache_pressure_denom __read_mostly = 100;
 
 unsigned long vfs_pressure_ratio(unsigned long val)
diff --git a/mm/page-writeback.c b/mm/page-writeback.c
index 123456789032..123456789033 100644
--- a/mm/page-writeback.c
+++ b/mm/page-writeback.c
@@ -72,7 +72,10 @@
 /*
  * Start background writeback (via writeback threads) at this percentage
  */
-static int dirty_background_ratio = 10;
+/* MicroVM: start background writeback sooner so dirty pages become
+ * clean (hence droppable/balloonable) sooner. Tunable via
+ * /proc/sys/vm/dirty_background_ratio. */
+static int dirty_background_ratio = 1;
 
 /*
  * dirty_background_bytes starts at 0 (disabled) so that it is a function of
@@ -89,7 +92,9 @@
 /*
  * The generator of dirty data starts writeback at this percentage
  */
-static int vm_dirty_ratio = 20;
+/* MicroVM: throttle dirty generators sooner; dirty pages pin host
+ * memory until writeback. Tunable via /proc/sys/vm/dirty_ratio. */
+static int vm_dirty_ratio = 2;
 
 /*
  * vm_dirty_bytes starts at 0 (disabled) so that it is a function of
diff --git a/mm/page_alloc.c b/mm/page_alloc.c
index 123456789034..123456789035 100644
--- a/mm/page_alloc.c
+++ b/mm/page_alloc.c
@@ -6571,10 +6571,17 @@
 	int new_min_free_kbytes;
 
 	lowmem_kbytes = nr_free_buffer_pages() * (PAGE_SIZE >> 10);
-	new_min_free_kbytes = int_sqrt(lowmem_kbytes * 16);
+	/*
+	 * MicroVM: quarter the stock sqrt(lowmem*16) reserve. Watermark
+	 * reserves are unballoonable; on 128-1024 MiB guests this frees
+	 * ~2-3 MiB of host RSS. Fresh microVMs boot with empty caches,
+	 * so the smaller reserve is safe.
+	 * (Tunable at runtime via /proc/sys/vm/min_free_kbytes.)
+	 */
+	new_min_free_kbytes = int_sqrt(lowmem_kbytes * 16) / 4;
 
 	if (new_min_free_kbytes > user_min_free_kbytes)
-		min_free_kbytes = clamp(new_min_free_kbytes, 128, 262144);
+		min_free_kbytes = clamp(new_min_free_kbytes, 128, 65536);
 	else
 		pr_warn("min_free_kbytes is not updated to %d because user defined value %d is preferred\n",
 				new_min_free_kbytes, user_min_free_kbytes);

-- 
2.47.0
